    "distinct_hypotheses": 414,
    "hypothesis": "The low-vol relative-strength carry can be sharpened by selecting names whose recent relative strength is monotonically improving across multiple short horizons, ensuring the institutional accumulation is still in its early phase rather than already extended. A stock that is strong over 20 days but not yet strong over 5 days is typically in the midst of a progressive inflow from volatility-targeting funds and other systematic buyers, who rebalance gradually as the trend develops. This timing filter should reduce exposure to names whose strength is already fully reflected, improving the sustainability of the carry while retaining the core low-vol and medium-term strength signal.",
